                  <img src="templates/millenniumFalcon/images/spacer.gif" height="3"><br>
                  &nbsp;<a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=11546&amp;sid=cc100c4a9f4e9ebb4fb7568cd6a69485"><img src="templates/millenniumFalcon/images/icon_quote_lang.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;
                  </td>
                <td valign="top" class="row2"> <span class="smalltext"><b>Galaxies</b></span>
                  <p><span class="largetext">This forum needs a Galaxies thread.
<br />

<br />
I've been following the game's development, and it sounds promising, although I must admit, there are some issues that could cause problems.  Here are some major points...
<br />

<br />
1. You only get one character slot per server (10 servers to start).  That is a max of 10 characters unless you unlock a force slot (see below).  Their reasoning is that there will be WAY more data to store per character than in other on line games.  Large inventories, houses, completely customizable physical characterstics, etc.  This is worrysome to me, because MANY people in EQ have alts and mules.  In Star Wars, you get one character.  Now, on the bright side, you can change professions any time you want and retrain in another.  This is good, but I think we can all imagine how this will be problematic.  
<br />

<br />
2. Jedi.  I want to be one.  You want to be one.  Unfortunately, a TINY amount of people will actually get to be one.  You have to "earn" the right to unlock a second character slot, in which you can create a force sensitive character.  No one is exactly sure how to do this, but it will not be a simple quest, and it will not be the same for everyone.  So, if you play Galaxies, you must accept that you may never get the chance to be a Jedi.
<br />

<br />
3. There are different types of damage in the game.  Some are physical-based "wounds", others are mind-based (battle fatigue).  Certain damage types can ONLY be healed by certain professions.  For example battle fatigue can only be healed by an entertainer, such as you may find in a cantina.  This is an interesting idea.  Could it be annoying though?  Haven't we learned in EQ that is not such a great idea to have only certain classes be able to do majorly important things?  Makes one group slot automatic and makes some classes less needed.
<br />

<br />
4. There will be no space combat/exploration at launch.  This will be added later.  This doesn't bother me too much, but it is certainly something to note.  I mean, it is Star Wars.
<br />

<br />
These are just the things that stick out to me.  There are MANY good things to look forward to.  For instance, if you are on rebel faction, you might have a bounty put on your head.  If you are a jedi, you may wind up meeting a certain Sith lord, or even Boba Fett.</span><span class="smalltext"></span></p>
