                  Location: Michigan</span><br>
                  <img src="templates/millenniumFalcon/images/spacer.gif" height="3"><br>
                  &nbsp;<a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=12582&amp;sid=cc100c4a9f4e9ebb4fb7568cd6a69485"><img src="templates/millenniumFalcon/images/icon_quote_lang.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;
                  </td>
                <td valign="top" class="row2"> <span class="smalltext"><b></b></span>
                  <p><span class="largetext">Not much to say just yet Zas.  I've played about 5 total hours now and there are many unfinished things in the game.  From what I've seen I am intrigued.  The graphics are excellent, as is character creation.  The skill trees are very strong as well.  You can really create a unique character in look and skills.  
<br />

<br />
There are mission terminals, as well as NPC quest givers.
<br />

<br />
You can build structures
<br />

<br />
Object collision is dorky with respect to NPC's right now.  I watched a Stormtrooper patrol walk through the outer wall of Mos Espa last night.
<br />

<br />
There are moments of lag, awful lag.  Usually in combat, which I am sure you can guess is scary.  Luckily I am fighting things I can kill with one or two hits.
<br />

<br />
I've seen some complaints that it doesn't <span style="font-style: italic">FEEL</span> like Star Wars.  I agree with this assessment in some places.  For example, Corellia.  A planet mentioned but not seen in the movies.  So, when I look at it, I can't say it is a Star Wars city.   But, Tatooine cities feel very much like Star Wars to me.</span><span class="smalltext"></span></p>
                </td>
