                  &nbsp;<a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=12748&amp;sid=cc100c4a9f4e9ebb4fb7568cd6a69485"><img src="templates/millenniumFalcon/images/icon_quote_lang.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;
                  </td>
                <td valign="top" class="row2"> <span class="smalltext"><b></b></span>
                  <p><span class="largetext">No second key, since I am using the second key from my brother.  <img src="images/smiles/icon_smile.gif" alt="icon_smile.gif" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
Keep in mind, there is no space combat. There is no space at all.  And this is one of the biggest pre-release complaints since they plan to release space stuff in a future expansion.  They have an expansion determined before they even release the game.  Really comes accross as a money grab when you consider that this is Star Wars and not having space is really really silly.
<br />

<br />
As an update, I have played quite a bit over the past few days, and I can say that there are some potential FATAL flaws in the game.  First, the missions are almost all lame.  Most are delivery missions where you have to run and run and run to deliver something for a few credits.  Do one or two of these in a night and you struggle just to stay awake.  The planets are devoid of anything interesting outside the cities so you just run through nothingness until you get to your destination.  On top of this, many times you get to the destination and the NPC is not there.  Talk about a bitch.  Good thing though, at least half of the missions are broken and don't even give work, so it saves you from having to run anywhere.
<br />

<br />
Another problem is the lag.  It is just awful.  This must be fixed before release.  Combat lag is absurd.  Just completely unaceptable.  
<br />

<br />
And lastly, from what I've seen, there is very little "WOW" factor to this game.  Maybe its because I am a brazen, long-time MMORPG player, but I haven't seen a single thing that has invoked a sense of wonder in me.  No scripted events, no cool waterfalls, no famous NPC's at the local cantina, nothing.
<br />

<br />
This IS beta, so all of these complaints could disappear by launch.  I am just being the dutiful tester and reporting everything, but I am worried right now.  Since its beta 3, the feature set is in and they are in bug hunt mode.  This is bad.  They need WAY more content.  WAY WAY more.  From what I've heard, I believe they know this, so there is still hope.</span><span class="smalltext"></span></p>
